llama: a reduced head for the MTP drafter of qwen35

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

Our 4B ties the head to token_embd.weight, 248320 rows of 2560 columns. Every MTP draft step reads
all of it, 675 MB at Q8_0, which is 86 % of the 782 MB of a draft step. The drafter does not need
the whole vocabulary. quant/draftset.py gathers a frequency-ranked subset of the rows into three
tensors of the GGUF, and the MTP graph reads the subset instead.

The change is lossless. The subset decides only what the drafter can propose. The target model
verifies each proposed token against the full head, thus a token outside the subset is never
accepted wrongly, it is simply never proposed. Measured on the 2B on a host CPU, greedy, draft
depth 3, a complete answer at end of generation: the output is byte-identical with the full head
and with the subset, 205 tokens.

The three tensors, all optional, all read only by the MTP graph:

    blk.N.nextn.draft_head.weight  the gathered rows, in the type of the source head
    blk.N.nextn.draft_ids          the vocabulary index of each row, I32, the scatter index
    blk.N.nextn.draft_fill         one F32, the logit of every token outside the subset

The scatter. ggml_set_rows writes whole rows, thus the graph puts the logits in the transposed
shape [1, n_vocab] for the scatter and reshapes on both sides. At one output row both reshapes are
views, thus an MTP pass with more rows takes the full head. ggml_repeat_4d builds the background
from draft_fill, and the Hexagon backend supports REPEAT and SET_ROWS for these shapes, thus the
draft graph does not split.

Files:
    src/llama-arch.h            three LLM_TENSOR_NEXTN_DRAFT_* entries
    src/llama-arch.cpp          their names and their tensor info
    src/llama-model.h           three fields of llama_layer_nextn
    src/llama-model-loader.cpp  a buft probe for SET_ROWS and for REPEAT
    src/models/qwen35.cpp       the tensors at load, the reduced matmul and the scatter in build_mtp

The loader skips a tensor whose info says GGML_OP_NONE, thus the index and the fill tensors declare
the op that reads them. weight_buft_supported had no case for either op and its default aborts.

How to apply, from the llama.cpp root:

    git apply patches/draft-head/0001-llama-qwen35-reduced-mtp-draft-head.patch

A model without the three tensors takes the full head, thus the patch changes nothing for a GGUF
that quant/draftset.py has not processed.
